  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Capacity of Government of Kenya and Resilience of Vulnerable Border Communities to Enhance Peace and Security along Kenya-Somalia border.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to contribute to durable solutions for the migrant and host communities in Mandera, Wajir, Garissa and Lamu Counties of Kenya that border Somalia, affected by negative impacts of the displacement triggered by the civil war in Somalia and climate hazards in the region, and to promote peace and security along Kenya-Somalia border. The project will fulfil the objective by achieving two outcomes of enhancing community resilience and social cohesion and strengthening the capacity of the Government of Kenya (GoK) at borders.The initial phase of the project will include livelihood and psychosocial support to at-risk youth and returnees and sensitization of the County Governments and community leaders on community policing and reintegration and rehabilitation in order to strengthen their socio-economic inclusion and resilience. The second part will focus on enhancing capacity of the GoK authorities and border officials to better counter transnational threats and respond to health needs specific to vulnerable migrants crossing borders. It will also offer benefits of enhanced trust between communities and border authorities to promote peace in border communities.</narrative>
  </description>
